#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166603 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6e692dca-1bbc-59e7-999f-4acb806ddd38" :question/math-academy-id "e-8369" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =7\\arcsch(1-x),$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcsch x) = -\\dfrac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(1-x)) \\\\  & =7\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(1-x)) \\\\  & =7(-\\frac{1}{|1-x|\\sqrt{1+(1-x)^{2}}})\\cdot (1-x)^{′} \\\\  & =7(-\\frac{1}{|x-1|\\sqrt{1+1-2x+{x}^{2}}})\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{|x-1|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2x+2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166604 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/id #uuid "b4dd5d1a-eeae-58f5-b7a1-a6a20fb02df9" :question/math-academy-id "e-8370" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =  5\\arsech{2x},$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arsech x) = -\\dfrac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x) \\\\  & =5(-\\frac{1}{(2x)\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}})\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166605 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/id #uuid "83b6c061-a8fc-5628-a199-60196b904407" :question/math-academy-id "e-8371" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y = \\arcoth{e^x},$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcoth x) = \\dfrac{1}{1-x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-({e}^{x})^{2}}\\cdot ({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{e}^{2x}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1-{e}^{2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166606 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5e40340-35cf-50ee-8a0d-7eb873490693" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "8a1806e8-d99d-5107-aa63-0bf841cb44c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-8372" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $f(x) = \\sin{x} \\cdot \\arcsch{x},$ then $f'(x) = \\cos{x} \\arcsch{x} + g(x).$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIn this case, the expression for $f(x)$  is a product $u(x) \\cdot v(x)$ with $u(x) = \\sin{x}$ and $v(x) = \\arcsch{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+{{(-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}})}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x) = -\\dfrac{\\sin{x}}{|x|\\sqrt{1+x^2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525033 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0fd46de-1da2-5b10-a3af-605f35681790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-25x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0fd46de-1da2-5b10-a3af-605f35681790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-25x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524772} :answer-field/id #uuid "90e4a11a-c640-5a57-bedb-12194318e132" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbea2a23-d4e5-557d-b7b2-686dae2de058" :question/math-academy-id "q-313240" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\,\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(5x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(2\\,\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(5x)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(5x)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{(5x)\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}})\\cdot (5x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5e40340-35cf-50ee-8a0d-7eb873490693" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15d81d09-9d4d-5817-aef8-323fc9bab399" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4x-4{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15d81d09-9d4d-5817-aef8-323fc9bab399" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4x-4{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524423} :answer-field/id #uuid "697491e1-d5eb-582f-b6a9-c05cd0efc616" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7b99a120-8ee4-5c4d-80c5-2291fb8275da" :question/math-academy-id "q-313249" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)},$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\frac{1}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1).$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1))^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1))^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1))^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1))^{′}=\\frac{1}{1-(2x-1)^{2}}\\cdot (2x-1)^{′}=\\frac{2}{4x-4{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(4x-4{x}^{2})\\,{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4x-4{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{1}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63d9495c-c41d-5aa2-aeaa-a8b740540555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4x^{2}-12x+10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63d9495c-c41d-5aa2-aeaa-a8b740540555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4x^{2}-12x+10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524545} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4cb4e3c-90dc-5a4e-ad03-801bee72ca2f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7d0c5e9-6b20-5038-9084-51ca2beb31f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-341460" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-4\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(3-2x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{|3-2x|}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[-4\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(3-2x)] \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(3-2x)] \\\\  & =-4\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{|3-2x|\\sqrt{1+(3-2x)^{2}}}]\\cdot (3-2x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{|3-2x|\\sqrt{1+(9-12x+4{x}^{2})}}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|3-2x|}\\,\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{10-12x+4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93683338-b97b-5b47-8572-b2056cda9e98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{1+\\sqrt{x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93683338-b97b-5b47-8572-b2056cda9e98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{1+\\sqrt{x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524617} :answer-field/id #uuid "f068fa89-ce05-5148-b62a-30202a76bdb3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca1680c8-f47c-5b1b-8548-5d42d12634c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-341475" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{x}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $x>0.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{x})] \\\\  & =-2\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{|\\sqrt[4]{x}|\\sqrt{1+{(\\sqrt[4]{x})}^{2}}}]\\cdot {(\\sqrt[4]{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[4]{x}\\sqrt{1+\\sqrt{x}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt[4]{{x}^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{1+\\sqrt{x}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525059 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe2cbb58-2d32-596a-a5ab-d999b693990b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\ln 3}{\\sqrt{1-3^{2x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe2cbb58-2d32-596a-a5ab-d999b693990b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\ln 3}{\\sqrt{1-3^{2x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524838} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0fee573-85d6-5302-b91f-3a65063b3585" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0b7921b-6648-5449-80a2-dd554708f1c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-341516" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arsech}⁡({3}^{x}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arsech}⁡({3}^{x})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{3}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{({3}^{x})}^{2}}}\\cdot {({3}^{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{3}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{9}^{x}}}\\cdot {3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\sqrt{1-{9}^{x}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c22ce809-4a35-50df-baa6-93cca13a5284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x(x-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c22ce809-4a35-50df-baa6-93cca13a5284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x(x-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524693} :answer-field/id #uuid "4785fe34-e531-5b8c-856b-b1bf92d27631" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88d8545b-9874-55b6-990b-870f4aec4ac1" :question/math-academy-id "q-341522" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(1-x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(1-x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-(1-x)^{2}}\\cdot (1-x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-(1-2x+{x}^{2})}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2x-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x(x-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525039 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07693188-9e0b-5dc7-8381-dfa9941382ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07693188-9e0b-5dc7-8381-dfa9941382ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524396} :answer-field/id #uuid "20a149cb-038d-5c18-bde3-ae3a967e2c4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c6349a80-6bbd-5879-a48d-57a06b8a80ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-341524" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(-x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(-x)] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1-(-x)^{2}}\\cdot (-x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1-{x}^{2}}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea4045af-0bcf-5dbb-8afa-0d8bfbe1111c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1-x^{2/3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea4045af-0bcf-5dbb-8afa-0d8bfbe1111c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1-x^{2/3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524793} :answer-field/id #uuid "dffaf696-90ee-57c0-93f5-481258f07333" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "585fdeed-02dd-5444-8201-a19fa1a46351" :question/math-academy-id "q-341535" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{x}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2/3}}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[3\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{x})] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1-{(\\sqrt[3]{x})}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt[3]{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2/3}}\\frac{1}{(1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5e40340-35cf-50ee-8a0d-7eb873490693" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39c346e6-1707-5c7d-ba00-77662529622f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39c346e6-1707-5c7d-ba00-77662529622f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524486} :answer-field/id #uuid "584b1c26-caed-504f-b964-753688b3a2ed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3337e5e0-9e46-58ca-9b60-fe0a52d9614e" :question/math-academy-id "q-341550" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(x)}{\\sqrt{x}},$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}($ \n{{field-1}} $-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{2x})$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(x)$ and $v(x)=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{{[v(x)]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}-\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x\\cdot {(\\sqrt{x})}^{′}}{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x\\cdot {(\\sqrt{x})}^{′}}{x} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}})\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{2x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{2x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5e40340-35cf-50ee-8a0d-7eb873490693" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b29336a1-2d9f-50d2-a125-62f689031329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\ln x}{x\\sqrt{1-x^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b29336a1-2d9f-50d2-a125-62f689031329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\ln x}{x\\sqrt{1-x^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524670} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d13f910-7112-5195-9bff-e3f1ef20780b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54c54e62-4a18-5ab6-878d-ec4e2ae2aaa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-341554" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x,$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x}{x}\\,-$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a product $u(x)\\cdot v(x)$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsech}⁡x\\,+\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167378 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f805684-7c7e-5830-8bc2-33a31c975e08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{8}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524469} {:answer/id #uuid "67683680-de16-5a45-a98f-3994dc91a997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}(2-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{8}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524550} {:answer/id #uuid "7f39a794-3765-568c-9788-0c0859104a83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{x}(1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{8}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524582} {:answer/id #uuid "debe51b5-eeec-5077-a1f0-fbae0d3a18d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{x}(1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{8}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524762} {:answer/id #uuid "e839ce63-4bb9-53b7-a7ca-6fd8f3ee858e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{8}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f39a794-3765-568c-9788-0c0859104a83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{x}(1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{8}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524582} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d047628-3fed-5c7b-8f40-ea09ee24e00d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1ed5664-2642-587f-b8dc-ece93bd79695" :question/math-academy-id "q-95517" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{x}^{4},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}+(-\\frac{1}{|{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{1+({x}^{4})^{2}}})\\cdot ({x}^{4})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{8}}}\\cdot 4{x}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{4}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{8}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}(1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{8}}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525057 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07099b62-b5de-5c35-89a0-02da7d237dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}(1-\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524394} {:answer/id #uuid "109c4078-1dc2-5f49-97cd-be914eaf3edf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}(1+\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524411} {:answer/id #uuid "92f271ed-bbcd-5ac7-8f4f-93ee8ccc4ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}(1+\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524614} {:answer/id #uuid "99e51ccf-d968-5c52-81a9-7aa43ff31aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}(1-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524629} {:answer/id #uuid "c136c3e1-1248-5b47-b929-510459d6c30b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}(1-\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07099b62-b5de-5c35-89a0-02da7d237dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}(1-\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524394} :answer-field/id #uuid "7230352a-4cad-516b-aa5e-9529af383602" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ee2856c4-f82b-5153-9418-e0c2792ce17b" :question/math-academy-id "q-95519" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({x}^{2}+1),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}+(-\\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}+1|\\sqrt{1+({x}^{2}+1)^{2}}})\\cdot ({x}^{2}+1)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+1)\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+1}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}(1-\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525026 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "121480c5-f561-5438-8bde-1acc56bc6ff3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{|3x-1|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524413} {:answer/id #uuid "19520b3d-6125-58b2-9903-4c322a050cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{|3x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524428} {:answer/id #uuid "3cf94dd4-3101-57df-8fb6-af244a85af6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{|3x-1|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524496} {:answer/id #uuid "7609ee66-97eb-5813-aafc-fc892436fd47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{|3x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524570} {:answer/id #uuid "9773a4e4-9e61-5